S="Advent: Getting Ready"
D("2026-12-07",S,"Fire from Heaven","an older kid","1 Kings 18:39",[(39,"And when all the people saw it, they fell on their faces and said, “The LORD, he is God; the LORD, he is God.”")],
"Elijah on Mount Carmel",[
"Israel had a wicked king named Ahab, who worshiped a fake god called Baal. God sent His prophet Elijah to challenge Baal’s 450 prophets on Mount Carmel. “Let’s each build an altar and put a sacrifice on it. Don’t light the fire. The God who answers by fire, He is God.”",
"The prophets of Baal went first. From morning until noon they shouted, “O Baal, answer us!” They danced and yelled. Nothing happened. Elijah teased them: “Shout louder! Maybe he’s asleep!” They shouted all afternoon. Still nothing. No voice. No answer.",
"Then Elijah rebuilt the Lord’s altar with twelve stones and had the people pour water over it, three times, until it was soaked and the trench was full. Then Elijah prayed a simple prayer: “Lord, let them know that You are God.” Fire fell from heaven and burned up the sacrifice, the wood, the stones, and even the water! The people fell on their faces: “The Lord, He is God!”"],
"Elijah and Advent",["The very last Old Testament book, Malachi, promised God would send “Elijah” before the Lord came. Jesus said John the Baptist was that Elijah, the one who would get people ready for Jesus. That’s why Elijah shows up in Advent."],
["How many prophets of Baal were there? What did Elijah pour on his altar?","Why did Elijah have them pour water on the altar?","Baal never answered because he wasn’t real. What “fake gods” do people trust in today?"],
"Lord God, You alone are God, and You answer when we pray. Thank You for sending prophets like Elijah to call people back to You.","Turn our hearts away from fake gods and toward You.",
"Elijah prayed, and God sent fire from heaven! The people shouted, “The Lord, He is God!”",
["The fake god was named [Baal].","Elijah met them on Mount [Carmel].","Elijah poured [water] on his altar.","God sent [fire] from heaven.","The people said, “The Lord, He is [God]!”"],
["ELIJAH","FIRE","ALTAR","BAAL","CARMEL","WATER"],[("Did Baal answer?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who sent the fire?",["The Lord","Elijah"],0)],
"Draw fire falling from heaven on Elijah’s altar.",("1 Kings 18:39","“The LORD, he is God.”"),
scene(mountains(),altar(320),'<path d="M300,60 L280,120 L300,120 L276,180 M340,60 L360,120 L340,120 L364,180" fill="none" stroke-width="2"/>',person(170,beard=True,arms="up",hair="wrap"),person(500,beard=True,arms="open",hair="short",s=.8),label="Coloring picture: Elijah and fire falling on the altar"))

D("2026-12-08",S,"Zechariah Can’t Talk","a 3rd–5th grader","Luke 1:13",[(13,"But the angel said to him, “Do not be afraid, Zechariah, for your prayer has been heard, and your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you shall call his name John.")],
"An angel in the temple",[
"An old priest named Zechariah and his wife Elizabeth loved God, but they had no children, and now they were too old. One day Zechariah was chosen to go into the holy place of the temple to burn incense, something a priest might get to do only once in his whole life.",
"Suddenly, right beside the altar, stood an angel! Zechariah was terrified. The angel said, “Don’t be afraid. Your prayer has been heard. Elizabeth will have a son, and you will name him John. He will get people ready for the Lord.” Zechariah said, “How can I be sure? We’re too old!”",
"The angel answered, “I am Gabriel. I stand in the presence of God. Because you didn’t believe, you won’t be able to speak until it happens.” When Zechariah came out, he couldn’t say a word. He could only wave his hands. But God kept His promise: Elizabeth was going to have a baby."],
"God hears prayers",["Zechariah had prayed for a child for years, maybe so long he’d given up. But God had heard every prayer. God’s timing isn’t ours. And this baby, John, would be the one to point to Jesus."],
["What was the angel’s name? What would the baby be named?","Why couldn’t Zechariah talk?","Zechariah had prayed for many years. Why do you think God waited? Is there something you’ve prayed about for a long time?"],
"Heavenly Father, thank You for hearing every prayer, even ones we’ve almost given up on. Thank You for sending John to get people ready for Jesus.","Give us faith to believe Your promises.",
"The angel Gabriel told Zechariah he would have a son named John. Zechariah couldn’t talk until it happened!",
["Zechariah was a [priest].","His wife was [Elizabeth].","The angel’s name was [Gabriel].","Their baby would be named [John].","Zechariah couldn’t [speak]."],
["GABRIEL","JOHN","TEMPLE","INCENSE","PRIEST","ANGEL"],[("Did Zechariah believe the angel right away?",["Yes","No"],1),("Did God hear Zechariah’s prayers?",["Yes","No"],0)],
"Draw Zechariah in the temple with the angel.",("Luke 1:13","“Do not be afraid, Zechariah, for your prayer has been heard.”"),
scene(temple(),angel(420,.85),person(220,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="wrap"),'<path d="M300,300 v-30 h24 v30 M296,270 h32 M312,262 q-6,-16 0,-30 q6,14 0,30" />',label="Coloring picture: the angel Gabriel appearing to Zechariah in the temple"))

D("2026-12-09",S,"Let It Be to Me","an older kid","Luke 1:30–31, 38",[(30,"And the angel said to her, “Do not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God."),(31,"And behold, you will conceive in your womb and bear a son, and you shall call his name Jesus."),(38,"And Mary said, “Behold, I am the servant of the Lord; let it be to me according to your word.” And the angel departed from her.")],
"Gabriel visits Mary",[
"Six months later, God sent Gabriel again, this time to a little town called Nazareth, to a young woman named Mary. She was engaged to marry a carpenter named Joseph, from King David’s family. Gabriel said, “Greetings, favored one! The Lord is with you!” Mary was confused. What could this mean?",
"“Don’t be afraid, Mary. You will have a son, and you will name Him Jesus. He will be great, the Son of the Most High. He will sit on David’s throne, and His kingdom will never end.” Mary asked, “How can this be, since I’m not married?” Gabriel said, “The Holy Spirit will come upon you. The child will be called the Son of God. Nothing is impossible with God.”",
"Mary could have argued or been scared. Instead, she said, “I am the Lord’s servant. Let it be to me as you have said.” Mary trusted God’s Word. And right then, God’s Son began to grow inside her. God was becoming a human being."],
"Nothing is impossible",["Zechariah asked, “How can I be sure?” Mary asked, “How will this happen?” and then she believed. Mary’s faith wasn’t in herself. It was in God’s Word. That’s our faith too: “Let it be to me according to Your word.”"],
["What town did Mary live in? What name did Gabriel say to give the baby?","What did Mary say after the angel explained?","Mary’s answer is a model of faith. What makes it different from Zechariah’s? What would it look like to say “let it be to me” in your own life?"],
"Lord God, nothing is impossible with You. Thank You for Mary’s faith, and for sending Your Son to be born as one of us.","Give us faith to say, “Let it be to me according to Your word.”",
"The angel Gabriel told Mary she would be the mother of Jesus. Mary said, “I am the servant of the Lord!”",
["Mary lived in [Nazareth].","She was going to marry [Joseph].","The baby would be named [Jesus].","Nothing is [impossible] with God.","Mary said, “I am the [servant] of the Lord.”"],
["MARY","GABRIEL","NAZARETH","JESUS","SERVANT","FAVOR"],[("Did Mary trust God’s word?",["Yes","No"],0),("Is anything impossible with God?",["Yes","No"],1)],
"Draw Mary and the angel Gabriel.",("Luke 1:38","“Behold, I am the servant of the Lord.”"),
scene(window(80),angel(420),person(220,beard=False,arms="open",hair="wrap"),'<path d="M90,300 h80 v-40 h-80 Z" />',label="Coloring picture: the angel Gabriel visiting Mary"))

D("2026-12-10",S,"The Baby Who Jumped","a K–2nd grader, with help","Luke 1:46–47",[(46,"And Mary said, “My soul magnifies the Lord,"),(47,"and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior,")],
"Mary visits Elizabeth",[
"After the angel’s visit, Mary hurried to the hill country to visit her relative Elizabeth, who was going to have baby John. It was a long trip, but Mary couldn’t wait to see her.",
"When Mary walked in and said hello, something amazing happened: baby John jumped inside Elizabeth! The Holy Spirit filled Elizabeth, and she shouted, “Blessed are you among women, and blessed is the baby you carry! Why am I so honored that the mother of my Lord comes to me?” Even before he was born, John was already rejoicing about Jesus!",
"Mary was so full of joy that she sang a song. It begins, “My soul magnifies the Lord, and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior.” She sang about how God lifts up the humble and fills the hungry with good things. The church still sings Mary’s song, called the Magnificat, at evening prayer."],
"Joy",["John wasn’t born yet, but he already knew Jesus was near. Babies, even unborn babies, are precious to God. And Jesus brings joy to everyone near Him."],
["Who did Mary visit? What did baby John do?","What did Elizabeth call Mary’s baby?","Mary called God “my Savior.” Why did even Mary need a Savior? What does it mean to “magnify” the Lord?"],
"Lord God, our souls magnify You and our spirits rejoice in You, our Savior. Thank You for every baby, born and unborn.","Fill us with the joy of Jesus this Advent.",
"Baby John jumped for joy inside Elizabeth when Mary came to visit! Mary sang a song of praise.",
["Mary visited [Elizabeth].","Baby John [jumped] for joy.","Elizabeth called Jesus “my [Lord].”","Mary sang, “My soul [magnifies] the Lord.”","Mary called God her [Savior]."],
["MARY","JOY","SONG","JUMP","ELIZABETH","SAVIOR"],[("Did baby John know Jesus was near?",["Yes","No"],0),("What did Mary do?",["Sang a song","Went home sad"],0)],
"Draw Mary and Elizabeth hugging.",("Luke 1:47","“My spirit rejoices in God my Savior.”"),
scene(hills(),house(500),person(220,beard=False,arms="open",hair="wrap"),person(310,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short"),sun(80,60),label="Coloring picture: Mary visiting Elizabeth"))

D("2026-12-11",S,"His Name Is John","a 3rd–5th grader","Luke 1:63–64",[(63,"And he asked for a writing tablet and wrote, “His name is John.” And they all wondered."),(64,"And immediately his mouth was opened and his tongue loosed, and he spoke, blessing God.")],
"John is born",[
"The day came, and Elizabeth had her baby boy. All the neighbors and relatives were so happy for her. Eight days later, they gathered to name him. Everyone said, “Call him Zechariah, after his father.”",
"But Elizabeth said, “No. His name is John.” “But nobody in your family has that name!” So they made signs to Zechariah, who still couldn’t talk. He asked for a writing tablet and wrote: “His name is John.” Everyone was amazed.",
"And at that very moment, Zechariah could talk again! The first thing he did was praise God. He sang a song, filled with the Holy Spirit: “Blessed be the Lord God of Israel, for He has visited and redeemed His people!” Then he looked at his baby son: “And you, child, will be called the prophet of the Most High. You will go before the Lord to prepare His ways.”"],
"Prepare the way",["Zechariah’s song, the Benedictus, is sung in the church’s morning prayer. John’s whole job in life was to point to Jesus. That’s a good job for us, too."],
["What did everyone want to name the baby? What did Zechariah write?","What was the first thing Zechariah did when he could talk again?","John’s job was to “prepare the way” for Jesus. How can we point others to Jesus?"],
"Blessed be the Lord God of Israel, for He has visited and redeemed His people! Thank You for giving Zechariah his voice back to praise You.","Use our voices to praise You and point others to Jesus.",
"Zechariah wrote, “His name is John!” and he could talk again. He sang praise to God!",
["Elizabeth had a baby [boy].","People wanted to name him [Zechariah].","Zechariah wrote, “His name is [John].”","Then Zechariah could [talk] again.","John would [prepare] the way for Jesus."],
["JOHN","TABLET","NAME","PRAISE","BLESSED","PROPHET"],[("What was the first thing Zechariah did when he could talk?",["Praised God","Complained"],0),("Whose way would John prepare?",["Jesus’","His own"],0)],
"Draw Zechariah writing on his tablet, “His name is John.”",("Luke 1:64","“He spoke, blessing God.”"),
scene(house(520),person(160,beard=True,arms="up",hair="wrap"),'<rect x="200" y="150" width="60" height="44" rx="3"/><path d="M210,166 h40 M210,178 h30" fill="none" stroke-width="1.2"/>',person(330,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short"),'<ellipse cx="330" cy="200" rx="20" ry="10"/><circle cx="346" cy="196" r="7"/>',label="Coloring picture: Zechariah writing John’s name"))

D("2026-12-12",S,"Joseph’s Dream","an older kid","Matthew 1:20–21",[(20,"But as he considered these things, behold, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream, saying, “Joseph, son of David, do not fear to take Mary as your wife, for that which is conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."),(21,"She will bear a son, and you shall call his name Jesus, for he will save his people from their sins.”")],
"Joseph trusts God",[
"Joseph the carpenter was engaged to Mary. When he found out she was going to have a baby, he was heartbroken and confused. He knew it wasn’t his baby. Joseph was a good man, and he didn’t want to embarrass Mary, so he decided to break off the engagement quietly.",
"But while he was thinking about it, an angel came to him in a dream. “Joseph, son of David, don’t be afraid to take Mary as your wife. The baby is from the Holy Spirit. She will have a son, and you will name Him Jesus, because He will save His people from their sins.” The name Jesus means “The Lord saves.”",
"When Joseph woke up, he did exactly what the angel said. He married Mary and took care of her. When the baby was born, Joseph named Him Jesus. The Bible never records a single word Joseph spoke. But it tells us over and over what he did: he trusted and obeyed."],
"Quiet faith",["Joseph is a great example for dads, and for everyone. He didn’t make speeches. He listened to God and did what God said, protecting Mary and Jesus. God chose Joseph to be Jesus’ earthly father."],
["What did the angel tell Joseph in his dream? What does the name Jesus mean?","Joseph was confused and hurt at first. How did he show faith?","The Bible records none of Joseph’s words, only his actions. What does quiet, obedient faith look like at home?"],
"Lord God, thank You for Joseph, who trusted You and protected Mary and Jesus. Thank You for Jesus, who saves us from our sins.","Give our family quiet, faithful hearts that listen and obey.",
"An angel told Joseph in a dream, “Name the baby Jesus, for He will save His people from their sins.”",
["Joseph was a [carpenter].","An angel came to him in a [dream].","The angel said, “Don’t be [afraid].”","The baby would be named [Jesus].","Jesus will save His people from their [sins]."],
["JOSEPH","DREAM","ANGEL","JESUS","SAVE","CARPENTER"],[("Did Joseph obey the angel?",["Yes","No"],0),("What does the name Jesus mean?",["The Lord saves","Little king"],0)],
"Draw Joseph asleep, dreaming of the angel.",("Matthew 1:21","“He will save his people from their sins.”"),
scene(moon(80,60),stars(8,51,(200,640)),'<path d="M90,300 V266 H330 V300 M90,266 q0,-20 30,-20 h40 v20" />','<ellipse cx="150" cy="258" rx="20" ry="12"/><path d="M170,262 q80,-24 150,0" />',angel(470,.85),'<path d="M380,300 v-24 h60 v24 M376,276 h68" />',label="Coloring picture: Joseph dreaming of an angel"))

D("2026-12-13",S,"Behold, the Lamb of God","Mom or Dad","Isaiah 40:3; John 1:29",[("Isa 40:3","A voice cries: “In the wilderness prepare the way of the LORD; make straight in the desert a highway for our God."),("John 1:29","The next day he saw Jesus coming toward him, and said, “Behold, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!")],
"John the Baptist",[
"Today is the third Sunday of Advent. Baby John grew up and went to live in the wilderness. He wore clothes of camel’s hair and ate locusts and wild honey! He was the voice Isaiah promised, crying in the wilderness, “Prepare the way of the Lord!”",
"Crowds came out from the cities to hear him. John told them, “Repent! Turn away from your sins, because the kingdom of heaven is near.” People confessed their sins, and John baptized them in the Jordan River. Some people wondered, “Is John the Christ?” But John said, “No. Someone is coming who is greater than I am. I’m not even worthy to untie His sandals.”",
"Then one day, John saw Jesus walking toward him. John pointed and shouted, “Behold, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!” That was John’s whole job: point to Jesus. “He must increase, but I must decrease.”"],
"Pointing to Jesus",["We sing John’s words in church before the Lord’s Supper: “Lamb of God, You take away the sin of the world; have mercy on us.” Advent is a time to repent and get ready, like John said, because the Lamb is coming."],
["What did John eat? Where did he baptize people?","What did John say when he saw Jesus?","John said, “He must increase, but I must decrease.” What does that mean for us?"],
"Lamb of God, You take away the sin of the world; have mercy on us. Thank You for John, who pointed the way to You.","Prepare our hearts this Advent to receive You.",
"John the Baptist pointed to Jesus and said, “Behold, the Lamb of God!”",
["John lived in the [wilderness].","He ate locusts and wild [honey].","He baptized people in the [Jordan] River.","John said, “Prepare the [way] of the Lord!”","Jesus is the [Lamb] of God."],
["JOHN","JORDAN","BAPTIZE","LOCUSTS","HONEY","LAMB"],[("Was John the Christ?",["Yes","No"],1),("What was John’s job?",["Point to Jesus","Become famous"],0)],
"Draw John the Baptist pointing to Jesus.",("John 1:29","“Behold, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!”"),
scene(mountains(),waves(276,200,636),person(140,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="curly"),person(420,beard=True,arms="open",hair="short"),lamb(560),wreath(560,3) if False else '',label="Coloring picture: John the Baptist pointing to Jesus at the Jordan River"))
